I now have a complete picture. Here is my thorough report.

## Summary

The repository is a Spring Boot PetClinic variant. There is ONE write endpoint of interest, `POST /api/owners`, in `OwnerRestControllerV1`. Importantly: **the current implementation does NOT match what the acceptance test expects.** The current `identityKey` is a plain pipe-joined string (`telephone|email|householdId`), and **there is no soundex implementation anywhere in the codebase** — the word "soundex" appears only in the acceptance test's Javadoc describing the *desired* "identity-key-v2" behavior. Details below.

---

## 1. Files that compute identityKey and householdId

### identityKey — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

This is the single source of truth for the key (used both on the DTO and by the 409 check). Lines 195-199:

```java
default String toIdentityKey(Owner owner) {
    String email = hasEmail(owner) ? owner.getEmail() : "";
    String household = owner.getHouseholdId() == null ? "" : owner.getHouseholdId();
    return owner.getTelephone() + "|" + email + "|" + household;
}
```

Note: this is a plain `telephone|email|household` string — NOT a SHA-256 hex, NOT soundex-based. The acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java`) expects a 64-char lowercase hex `[0-9a-f]{64}` computed as `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))`. The current code will fail that test.

### householdId — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`

`assignHousehold` (lines 271-274) plus private helpers `normalizeForHousehold` (284-289) and `householdIdFor` (302-315):

```java
@Override
public void assignHousehold(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdIdFor(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()));
}

private static String normalizeForHousehold(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return "";
    }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}

private static String householdIdFor(String lastName, String postcode) {
    String key = normalizeForHousehold(lastName) + "|" + (postcode == null ? "" : postcode);
    try {
        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
            .digest(key.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(digest.length * 2);
        for (byte b : digest) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02X", b));
        }
        return sb.substring(0, 12);   // first 12 UPPER-case hex chars
    } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException ex) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 not available", ex);
    }
}
```

`isHouseholdInUse` (lines 251-269) skips deleted owners and an optional excludeId, returns true if any live owner shares the householdId.

---

## 2. Duplicate detection (409), email blocklist, deleted flag, soft match

All in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.

### 409 duplicate detection — `isIdentityKeyInUse` (lines 765-778), called from `addOwner` at lines 165-168:

```java
if (isIdentityKeyInUse(ownerMapper.toIdentityKey(owner), null)) {
    throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
        "an owner with the same identity already exists");
}
```

```java
private boolean isIdentityKeyInUse(String identityKey, Integer excludeId) {
    for (Owner existing : this.clinicService.findAllOwners()) {
        if (existing.isDeleted()) {
            continue;
        }
        if (excludeId != null && excludeId.equals(existing.getId())) {
            continue;
        }
        if (identityKey.equals(ownerMapper.toIdentityKey(existing))) {
            return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```

(There is a second 409 in `addOwner` at lines 169-172 for city capacity — likely not what you mean, but noting it.)

### Email-domain blocklist — `normalizeEmail` (lines 604-634):

```java
private static final Set<String> DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS =
    Set.of("mailinator.com", "tempmail.com", "guerrillamail.com");

private static String normalizeEmail(String email) {
    if (email == null) {
        return null;
    }
    if (!EMAIL_PATTERN.matcher(email).matches()) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
            "email must be a syntactically valid address");
    }
    String normalized = email.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    String domain = normalized.substring(normalized.indexOf('@') + 1);
    if (DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS.contains(domain)) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
            "email domain " + domain + " is not allowed");
    }
    return normalized;
}
```

`EMAIL_PATTERN` is defined at line 597: `^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$`.

### "deleted" owner flag handling

- Entity field: `Owner.deleted` (see section 5).
- Soft delete in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` `deleteOwner` (lines 144-150):
```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void deleteOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    // Soft delete: flag the owner deleted and retain the row rather than removing it.
    owner.setDeleted(true);
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```
- Deleted owners are skipped by `isIdentityKeyInUse` (line 767), `isHouseholdInUse` (ClinicServiceImpl line 258), and `findPossibleDuplicate` (line 796).
- The controller `deleteOwner` (lines 217-227) delegates to the service.

### Soft-match logic — `findPossibleDuplicate` (lines 791-802), called at lines 182-185:

```java
boolean declaredHouseholdMember = sharesHousehold && householdInUse;
Owner softDuplicate = declaredHouseholdMember ? null : findPossibleDuplicate(owner);
owner.setPossibleDuplicate(softDuplicate != null);
owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(softDuplicate == null ? null : softDuplicate.getId());
```

```java
private Owner findPossibleDuplicate(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getLastName() == null || owner.getPostcode() == null) {
        return null;
    }
    return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())
        .filter(existing -> owner.getLastName().equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getLastName()))
        .filter(existing -> owner.getPostcode().equals(existing.getPostcode()))
        .filter(existing -> !owner.getTelephone().equals(existing.getTelephone()))
        .min(Comparator.comparingInt(Owner::getId))
        .orElse(null);
}
```

So a "soft match" = same last name (case-insensitive) + same postcode + DIFFERENT telephone (a hard/identity duplicate would already have been rejected with 409). Lowest id wins for determinism.

The `sharesHousehold` write-only flag comes from `OwnerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold()` (line 157). When set and the household already exists, the owner is admitted as a declared household member and NOT flagged as a possible duplicate.

---

## 3. Helpers for normalizing telephone, lowercasing email, soundex

- **Normalize telephone** → `normalizeTelephone` (OwnerRestControllerV1 lines 552-567) plus `validateNationalNumberLength` (579-590). Strips `[\s\-()]`, assumes `+61` when no `+`, drops a leading `0`, requires `+` then 8-15 digits, and enforces per-country national-digit length.
- Supporting table: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/E164PhoneNumbers.java` — `NATIONAL_LENGTHS = {"61":9, "1":10}` and `countryCode(digits)` (longest-prefix match).
- **Lowercase email** → `normalizeEmail` (lines 619-634, shown above; `email.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT)`).
- **Soundex** → **DOES NOT EXIST.** No soundex helper anywhere in `src/main`. The only occurrence of the word is the Javadoc comment at the top of `AcceptanceTest.java` describing the intended v2 key. If you need soundex, it must be implemented (there is no Apache Commons Codec `Soundex` import either).

Also relevant (SHA-256 helpers you'd likely reuse for a hashed key): `sha256UpperHex` in OwnerRestControllerV1 (lines 349-361), and the test-side `sha256hex`/`shaHex` in AcceptanceBase (lines 282-299, note: LOWER-case hex in `sha256hex`).

---

## 4. Relevant test files

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the key one. Two tests:
  - `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`: asserts `identityKey` matches `[0-9a-f]{64}` (64-char lowercase hex).
  - `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity`: two owners with identical telephone/email/lastName → expects 409.
  - The class Javadoc (lines 9-11) states the target algorithm: `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box MockMvc scaffolding: payload builders (`ownerNode`, `structuredOwner`, `withPostcode`, `knownOwner`), request helpers (`createOwner`, `createOwnerOk`, `createOwnerWithKey`, `deleteOwner` soft-delete at lines 194-197, `fetchOwner`), unique generators, and computed-expectation helpers (`sha256hex` line 282, `shaHex` line 296, `luhn` line 302). `@Transactional` rollback + `@WithMockUser` admin.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — audit-log capture test util (references Owner; peripheral).

There are NO dedicated unit tests for `OwnerMapper.toIdentityKey`, `findPossibleDuplicate`, or household logic — coverage is only through the black-box acceptance tests.

---

## 5. Owner entity/model

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (`@Entity`, `@Table(name="owners")`, extends `Person` which supplies `firstName`/`lastName`). Fields relevant to your task (with getters/setters):

- `telephone` (line 55-58) — `@NotEmpty @Pattern("^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$")` E.164.
- `email` (60-61) — nullable.
- `postcode` (63-64).
- `householdId` (78-79) — `@Column(name="household_id")`.
- `deleted` (99-100) — `@Column(name="deleted", nullable=false) boolean deleted = false;` with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)`.
- `possibleDuplicate` (93-94) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (96-97) — the soft-match result fields.
- `namesakeCount`, `householdSize`, `membershipLevelCap`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate` — other create-time derived fields.

Note: **`identityKey` is NOT a persisted field on the entity** — it is derived at read time by `OwnerMapper.toIdentityKey` and only exposed on the DTO. `lastName` lives on the `Person` superclass at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`.

### DTO / OpenAPI contract

The DTO fields are generated from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`:
- `identityKey` (spec lines 2245-2257): documented as `telephone|email|householdId` joined with `|`, example `+61412345678||A1B2C3D4E5F6`. **This spec doc also does not match the acceptance test's SHA-256/soundex expectation** — so if you implement v2, both the spec and mapper need updating.
- `householdId` (2234-2244): "first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of normalized last name and postcode."
- `sharesHousehold` (2127-2138): write-only create flag.
- `possibleDuplicate` (2351+) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (2361+).

---

## Key discrepancy to flag

The acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java`) and its base describe an **"identity-key-v2"**: `identityKey = SHA-256 hex (64 lowercase hex chars) over normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)`. The current code produces a plain, unhashed `telephone|email|householdId` string and has **no soundex** anywhere. To satisfy the tests you would need to (a) add a soundex helper, (b) rewrite `OwnerMapper.toIdentityKey` to hash `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)` as lowercase SHA-256 hex, and (c) update the `identityKey` description in `openapi.yml`. The 409 duplicate check itself (`isIdentityKeyInUse`) already routes through `toIdentityKey`, so it would pick up the new key automatically.

