The acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java`) and its base describe an **"identity-key-v2"**: `identityKey = SHA-256 hex (64 lowercase hex chars) over normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)`. The current code produces a plain, unhashed `telephone|email|householdId` string and has **no soundex** anywhere. To satisfy the tests you would need to (a) add a soundex helper, (b) rewrite `OwnerMapper.toIdentityKey` to hash `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)` as lowercase SHA-256 hex, and (c) update the `identityKey` description in `openapi.yml`. The 409 duplicate check itself (`isIdentityKeyInUse`) already routes through `toIdentityKey`, so it would pick up the new key automatically.

